    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0217" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg135"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.34537/49.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-02-11"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 11, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 623.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence in
                    regard to the enlargement of our naval station at Guantánamo, I have the honor
                    to <pb facs="0218" n="136" xml:id="pg136"/> transmit herewith a copy and
                    translation of a confidential note dated the 8th instant which I received from
                    Sr. Sanguily, the Cuban secretary of state, last night * * *.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d154-f1"/></p>
                <p>The Secretary in this note refers to the treaty of 1904 in regard to the Isle of
                    Pines for the first time * * *.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Jackson.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d154-a1.xml" xpointer="d154-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d154-f1" n="1" xml:id="d154-f1-content">
                <p>The omissions appear under Naval Station at Guantánamo and Claim for the cost of
                    intervention in Cuba, <ref target="#pg118">pp. 118</ref> and <ref
                        target="#pg134">134</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
